<rml>
<head>
    <title>Vespera 2D / UI Foundation</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss" />
</head>
<body>
    <div id="root">
        <div id="header">
            <div>
                <div class="eyebrow">VESPERA 2D / UI FOUNDATION · EXPERIMENTAL</div>
                <div class="title">A real screen-space 2D starting point.</div>
            </div>
            <div id="score">Score 0</div>
        </div>

        <div id="playfield">
            <div class="grid-line grid-v1"></div>
            <div class="grid-line grid-v2"></div>
            <div class="grid-line grid-v3"></div>
            <div class="grid-line grid-h1"></div>
            <div class="grid-line grid-h2"></div>
            <div id="goal"></div>
            <div id="player"><div id="player-core"></div></div>
        </div>

        <div id="footer">
            <div>
                <div id="starter-status">Starting project C#...</div>
                <div class="note">WASD / arrows move · RmlUi is the 2D canvas · C# owns the game loop</div>
            </div>
            <button id="reset">Reset</button>
        </div>

        <div class="scope-note">Vespera 1.0 does not advertise a dedicated orthographic world editor. This template is intentionally a screen-space 2D/UI foundation using public RmlUi + C# APIs.</div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
